I'll implement `parseReport` using the `RowReader` capability since it's specifically designed for reading tab-delimited text. The implementation will handle quoted fields containing tabs by using the `RowReader` with a tab delimiter.

```kotlin
import org.test0.RowReader

fun parseReport(text: String): List<List<String>> {
    val reader = RowReader('\t')
    return reader.read(text)
}
```

This solution leverages the existing `RowReader` class which is designed exactly for this purpose - parsing tab-delimited text while properly handling quoted fields that may contain tabs. The implementation is concise and relies on the library's built-in functionality to handle all the parsing logic, including quoted fields.